# GHOSTNET local development hostnames.
# Source-of-truth for `scripts/hosts.{sh,ps1}` — those scripts copy the
# entries below (between the markers in your system hosts file) so every
# *.ghostnetw.test name resolves to 127.0.0.1.
#
# Why .test?  RFC 6761 reserves it for testing — it will never resolve
# via real DNS, so there's zero collision risk with anything on the open
# internet.
#
# Add a new hostname:
#   1. Append a line below.
#   2. Add a matching `reverse_proxy` block in dev/caddy/Caddyfile.
#   3. `npm run hosts:install` (or PowerShell variant on Windows).
#   4. `npm run caddy:reload`.

# ─── Public CDN ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
127.0.0.1   cdn.ghostnetw.test

# ─── Retro stack (Holo5 dev) ─────────────────────────────────────
127.0.0.1   retro.ghostnetw.test
127.0.0.1   assets.ghostnetw.test
127.0.0.1   swf.ghostnetw.test
127.0.0.1   arcturus.ghostnetw.test

# ─── .devcontainer web GUIs ──────────────────────────────────────
127.0.0.1   db.ghostnetw.test
127.0.0.1   pgadmin.ghostnetw.test
127.0.0.1   mail.ghostnetw.test
127.0.0.1   s3-console.ghostnetw.test
127.0.0.1   s3.ghostnetw.test
